.env.*.local
# Store state a `whip` run leaves in the working tree. The trailing `*` covers
# SQLite's `-wal` and `-shm` sidecars, which hold committed pages not yet
# checkpointed into the database file — every store opens in WAL mode, so they
# are always present next to a store that has been written.
#
# Scoped to the database files rather than the whole directory on purpose:
# `.whipplescript/skills/` is project content a user is meant to commit
# (spec/skills.md), and ignoring the directory would silently hide it.
**/.whipplescript/**/*.sqlite*
**/.whipplescript/*.sqlite*
.dev.vars
crates/whipplescript-host-do/worker/.wrangler/
